# hook sites of main (build DB93B0125F4850601D61C3EDDE012F8EB2ECFE77)
# frame rate (runtime games/fefw/fefw_play.cpp, [fefw] fps60): the gameplay start's target frame rate store `str w9, [x8, #0x1dc]`
# into the graphics object (w9 = 30, from `mov w9, #0x1e` at 0x71007bf1ac)
inline 0x71007bf1c0
# movies (runtime games/fefw/fefw_movie.cpp, [media] movies = host): the player's setup (0x1906510) picks native images or frames in CPU
# buffers by the byte at +0x1318 (`ldrb w21` at 0x190654c); the host decoder fills CPU buffers, so the site at the next instruction sets w21 = 1.
# On that path the player sets its frame count (+0xff8) to 4 only after making the buffers (2 by default, 0x1903ae0): the site before that sets it
# first (nxnative-penis6 patches.py does both by rewriting the code)
inline 0x7101906550
inline 0x7101906634
# frame update (runtime games/fefw/fefw_game.cpp, play mode): the present wrapper (nvnWindowSetPresentInterval, nvnQueuePresentTexture), once per
# presented frame on the main thread; it pumps play mode (window events, the gamepad into the npad state)
entryhook 0x710005d170
# time step (runtime games/fefw/fefw_play.cpp, [fefw] smooth_step, on with fps120): app::time::Manager's step (0x180eea0) before its clamp
# (`ldr s0, [x19, #0x168]`): s0 = the measured time since the last frame and s1 = the step the game chose (60 / target unless s0 is over it
# by 0.1), both in frames of 1/59.94 s; the hook may replace s1
inline 0x710180ef44
# map cursor (runtime games/fefw/fefw_play.cpp, [fefw] cursor_real_time): game::map::Cursor::Impl::Tick (0x735020) moves the battle / world map
# cursor by the stick times 5 * 60 / target frame rate (graphics +0x1dc) per frame; at each site s0 = 60 / target was just divided out
# (`fdiv s0, s1, s0`) and the hook may replace it with the frame's real step
inline 0x71007358b8
inline 0x7100735934
# ultrawide (runtime games/fefw/fefw_wide.cpp, [fefw] ultrawide). The camera, UI, scissor, marker, 2D-effect and movie sites follow Kompas9's
# MIT-licensed 3440x1440 IPS for this build (github.com/Kompas9/Switch-Game-Patches, games/Fire-Emblem-Fortunes-Weave); the picture / window
# and off-screen indicator sites are this port's. The runtime computes every value from the output's aspect.
# perspective camera update (0xb51420), after its prologue: x0 = the camera, its aspect as two floats at +0x70 / +0x74 (16, 9)
inline 0x7100b51440
# the 2D draw info's projection setter (0x5769d0): `ret` after the 4x4 matrix is copied to x0 + 0x10 (1920x1080 layouts: 1/960, -1/540)
inline 0x7100576a10
# nn::ui2d Picture::Calculate (0x595740) and Window::Calculate (0x5af080), after their LoadMtx (vtable + 0xf8) put the pane's global matrix
# into the draw info's model-view (+0x80) and before it goes to the pane's constant buffer: picture x19 / window x20 = the pane, the other
# the draw info. A pane covering the whole 1920 layout width (dims, backdrops) is widened there
inline 0x7100595784
